# .privacy-baseline — optional committed file for the required
# Privacy Guard commit-metadata check.
#
# A baseline is allowed only for historical exposure Benoît has
# accepted, recorded in the security-findings ledger. With this file
# present, the required check scans <sha>..HEAD on push (the SHA itself
# is excluded, as with git two-dot ranges). Pull requests still scan the
# PR range. A present but invalid file fails the check. With no file,
# the required check stays full-history.
#
# Copy to the repository root as .privacy-baseline. Use a full
# 40-character commit SHA. Do not put personal values in the reason.
#
# Required keys (no others):
sha: 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567
reason: accepted historical trailers; no rewrite
decided: 2026-11-22
